{"findings":[
{"rule":"J3","where":"Deployment._configureModules","severity":"HIGH","why":"The override runs the base setup, which restricts country 408, and then calls compliance.removeModule(countryModule). The country module is no longer bound to the compliance contract, so ModularCompliance.canTransfer never calls it and the restriction has no effect.","steps":"Deploy the setup. Call compliance.getModules(): only the MaxBalance module is listed. Call compliance.isModuleBound(countryModule): it returns false."},
{"rule":"J1","where":"Deployment._configureModules (removeModule of countryModule)","severity":"HIGH","why":"Wallet c is registered in restricted country 408 and holds a valid KYC claim. With the country module unbound, canTransfer checks only the max-balance module, so c can receive tokens.","steps":"agent calls token.mint(c, 100). It succeeds. Then a1 calls token.transfer(c, 10). It also succeeds."},
{"rule":"J2","where":"Deployment._configureModules (removeModule of countryModule)","severity":"HIGH","why":"Updating a wallet's country to 408 has no effect on transfers, because the country module is not consulted. A wallet moved to a restricted country can still receive tokens.","steps":"agent calls ir.updateCountry(b, 408). A holder then calls token.transfer(b, 10). It succeeds."}
]}
